  "description": "Power factor controllers with 5 or 7 outputs (RS485)",
  "revision": 2,
  "revised": "2026-10-16",
  "firmware_min": "8.9.5",
  "source": "BMR, \"FCR05/FCR07 Modbus registers\", file version 1.2",
  "sources": [{"title": "FCR05/FCR07 Modbus registers", "version": "1.2"}],
  "notes": [
    "BMR FCR05 / FCR07 power factor controllers, firmware 8.9.5 and newer.",
    "Every register is a float32. The manual gives no function code; this map reads them as holding registers (FC03) and writes them with FC16.",
    "Setting values with decimals are sent multiplied by 10 or 100 (a cos phi of 0.80 is sent as 80.0); the scale of each register undoes it.",
    "Enumerated settings use codes from 10000: 10001 is Off and 10002 is On.",
    "The manual gives no units for the powers, the stage operation counts or the stage on times.",
    "The alarm bits assume the low word of Active alarms is the second register, as for big word order."
  ],
  "protocol": "rtu",
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "big",
  "address_base": 0,
  "enums": {
    "off_on": {"10001": "Off", "10002": "On"},
    "stage_mode": {"10000": "Auto", "10001": "Off", "10002": "On"},
    "regulation_method": {"10000": "Square of the deviation", "10001": "Instantaneous cos phi", "10002": "APFR"},
    "parity": {"10001": "None", "10002": "Even", "10003": "Odd"}
  },
  "x_status": "official",
